## 4. Case Description

A 32-year-old male patient weighing 65 kg was diagnosed with acute bacterial sinusitis and prescribed tablet amoxicillin 500 mg three times daily for five days, starting on 01 March 2026.

On 03 March 2026, approximately two days after initiating treatment, the patient developed generalized itching and skin rashes over the chest.

Following the occurrence of the suspected adverse drug reaction, amoxicillin was discontinued on the same day. The patient was treated with antihistamines and recovered completely by 06 March 2026.

The temporal relationship between drug administration and the onset of the reaction raises suspicion of an amoxicillin-associated cutaneous adverse reaction.

## 5. ADR Identification

- **Suspected drug:** Amoxicillin
- **Adverse reaction:** Generalized itching and skin rash
- **Temporal association:** Reaction developed after initiation of amoxicillin.
- **Dechallenge:** Symptoms resolved following drug discontinuation and antihistamine treatment.
- **Rechallenge:** Not reported.
- **Alternative causes:** Insufficient information to determine.

**Identified suspected ADR:** Amoxicillin-associated skin reaction.

