## 10. Clinical Assessment

The patient developed generalized itching and skin rashes approximately two days after starting amoxicillin therapy.

The reaction improved following discontinuation of the suspected medicine and administration of antihistamines.

The clinical timeline supports a possible association between amoxicillin and the reported cutaneous reaction.

However, the absence of rechallenge information, detailed clinical examination, concomitant medication history, and evaluation of alternative causes limits the certainty of the causality assessment.

The event should be documented as a suspected adverse drug reaction rather than a confirmed drug allergy.

