## 12. Conclusion

This case describes a suspected adverse drug reaction associated with amoxicillin in a 32-year-old male patient treated for acute bacterial sinusitis.

The patient developed generalized itching and skin rashes two days after starting amoxicillin 500 mg three times daily. The suspected drug was discontinued, antihistamines were administered, and complete recovery occurred by 06 March 2026.

The Naranjo causality assessment produced a score of 3, indicating a **Possible** association.

Based on the information available, the reaction is provisionally classified as non-serious and expected, subject to verification against the applicable reference safety information.

This case highlights the importance of early ADR identification, appropriate documentation, causality assessment, and patient safety monitoring.

